	"description": "Model capability listings, replayed by _shared/lua/llm/model_capabilities.lua (macOS and Linux suites) and its AutoHotkey port _shared/modules/llm/model_capabilities.ahk (Windows suite), through the shipped thinking_off.json families and api_providers.json dialects.",
	"rule": "answers are recorded listing bodies (OpenRouter GET /models, Anthropic GET /v1/models, Gemini models.list), trimmed to a few models; the claude-opus-5, claude-haiku-5-5 and gemini-3.6-flash-image entries are synthetic negatives no current model shows (a type, a level or thinking listed as not supported). parse_vectors: the models a listing keeps (a model needs its id and, for OpenRouter, a supported_parameters array of strings; for Anthropic, a capabilities object; for Gemini, a boolean thinking), or the reason it is refused. lacks_vectors: a model lacks a control only when its listing says so: OpenRouter when a top-level field of the control's dialect template is not in supported_parameters; Anthropic when capabilities.thinking (or effort) is not supported, or its type (or level) is listed as not supported; Gemini when thinking is false. resolve_vectors: the request body after thinking_off resolution with the provider's listing (answers[provider]): a lacking control is skipped for the next one, kind absent when none applies. cache_vectors: one provider's cache from empty, its time to live capability_listing.ttl_hours of thinking_off.json: needs tells whether a fetch must start, begin marks one under way, finish stores the parsed answer of a listing (none: a failed fetch keeps the old records), records counts the models held.",
